## The two percentages in Rule 100(a)(2), derived rather than re-typed

<!-- l4: decide:an investor with income and net worth both -->

**18.** In relation to a NUMBER “x”, an investor with income and net worth both means InvestorProfile where name is probe, an accredited investor as defined in Rule 501 is FALSE, annual income is x, net worth is x and aggregate amount already sold to this investor across all issuers in reliance on section 4(a)(6) during the preceding 12 months is 0.

<!-- l4: decide:limb (i) probe -->

**19.** Limb (i) probe means the difference between 1 and income or net worth cut point.

<!-- l4: decide:limb (ii) probe -->

**20.** Limb (ii) probe means income or net worth cut point.

<!-- l4: decide:limb (i) percentage -->

**21.** Limb (i) percentage means the result of dividing the product of 100 and investment limit with an investor with income and net worth both with limb (i) probe by limb (i) probe.

<!-- l4: decide:limb (ii) percentage -->

**22.** Limb (ii) percentage means the result of dividing the product of 100 and investment limit with an investor with income and net worth both with limb (ii) probe by limb (ii) probe.

