**25.** In relation to a RaisePlan “plan”, blockers considered means list of PAIR with Your company is not organized under, and subject to, the laws of a US State or territory or the District of Columbia, so Regulation Crowdfunding is not available to it (17 CFR 227.100(b)(1)). and (b)(1) — not organized under State or territorial law with issuer profile from with plan, PAIR with Your company already files reports under section 13 or section 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, so it may not use Regulation Crowdfunding (17 CFR 227.100(b)(2)). and (b)(2) — an Exchange Act reporting company with issuer profile from with plan, PAIR with Your company is an investment company, or is excluded from that definition by section 3(b) or section 3(c) of the Investment Company Act of 1940, so it may not use Regulation Crowdfunding (17 CFR 227.100(b)(3)). and (b)(3) — an investment company with issuer profile from with plan, PAIR with Your company is subject to a bad-actor disqualification, so it may not offer or sell in reliance on section 4(a)(6) (17 CFR 227.100(b)(4), 227.503(a)). and (b)(4) — subject to a bad-actor disqualification with issuer profile from with plan, PAIR with Your company has sold under Regulation Crowdfunding before and has not filed the annual reports it owed in the two years before this offering statement, so it may not raise again until it has caught up (17 CFR 227.100(b)(5)). and (b)(5) — delinquent in ongoing annual reports with issuer profile from with plan, PAIR with Your company has no specific business plan, or its plan is to merge with or acquire a company it has not identified, so it may not use Regulation Crowdfunding (17 CFR 227.100(b)(6)). and (b)(6) — no specific business plan, or a blank-check business plan with issuer profile from with plan and PAIR with concatenate What you want to raise, added to what you have already sold under Regulation Crowdfunding in the last 12 months, comes to , dollars with aggregate for this raise with p