**27.** In relation to a RaisePlan “plan”, why those financial statements for means consider the case distinctions of financial statements required with offering from with plan :  when financial statements certified by the principal executive officer, with tax return information has  then concatenate Your raise aggregates to , dollars with aggregate for this raise with plan, , which is at or below the tier-1 ceiling of , dollars with tier 1 ceiling and , so financial statements certified by your principal executive officer, together with the tax return information the rule lists, are enough (17 CFR 227.201(t)(1)).. when financial statements reviewed by an independent public accountant has  then concatenate Your raise aggregates to , dollars with aggregate for this raise with plan, , above the tier-1 ceiling of , dollars with tier 1 ceiling, . A review by an independent public accountant is required up to , dollars with tier 2 ceiling, ; a first-time issuer may stay on a review up to , dollars with first-time issuer review ceiling and  (17 CFR 227.201(t)(2)-(3)).. when financial statements audited by an independent public accountant has  then concatenate Your raise aggregates to , dollars with aggregate for this raise with plan, , past the point at which a review will do: above , dollars with tier 2 ceiling,  a repeat issuer must be audited, and even a first-time issuer must be audited above , dollars with first-time issuer review ceiling and  (17 CFR 227.201(t)(3))..

<!-- l4: decide:what you must still line up -->

**28.** What you must still line up means list of Run the offering through exactly one intermediary — a registered broker or funding portal — that complies with section 4A(a) of the Securities Act, and conduct it exclusively on that intermediary's platform. Using more than one intermediary costs you the exemption (17 CFR 227.100(a)(3) and its Instruction)., concatenate Have your offering information publicly available on the intermediary's platform for at least , minimum days publicly available before any sale as string and  days before any securities are sold (17 CFR 227.303(a)(2))., File a Form C offering statement with the Commission, and provide it to investors and to the intermediary, before the offering begins. It must carry everything section 227.201 requires (17 CFR 227.203(a)(1))., The intermediary must deliver educational materials when it opens an investor's account, and must have a reasonable basis for believing each investor is within their own investment limits (17 CFR 227.302(b)(1), 227.303(b)(1)). Those are the intermediary's to satisfy, and this check does not ask about them. and Each investor must be within their own 12-month Regulation Crowdfunding limit (17 CFR 227.100(a)(2)). Use the investment-limit check for that..

<!-- l4: decide:after you raise you must -->

**29.** After you raise you must means list of concatenate File a Form C-AR annual report within , days to file the annual report after fiscal year end as string and  days of the end of each fiscal year, and keep filing until one of the five conditions in Rule 202(b) occurs (17 CFR 227.202(a), 227.203(b)(1))., concatenate Once one of those conditions occurs, file a Form C-TR within , business days to file Form C-TR as string and  business days to bring the reporting duty to an end (17 CFR 227.203(b)(3))., concatenate File a Form C-U progress update within , business days to file a progress update as string and  business days of reaching the relevant point in the offering (17 CFR 227.203(a)(3)(i)). and Miss the annual reports and you are disqualified from your NEXT Regulation Crowdfunding offering for two years (17 CFR 227.100(b)(5)) — though the default does not cost you the exemption for an offering already made (17 CFR 227.100(a)(4))..

<!-- l4: decide:raise caveats -->

**30.** Raise caveats means list of This check answers two of the four conditions in Rule 100(a): that your company is eligible, and that the raise is within the 12-month offering limit. The other two — the single complying intermediary, and each investor's own limit — are under 'what you must still line up'., The bad-actor disqualification is a single yes/no question here. Rule 503(a) is a regime in its own right: which people are covered, how far the look-back runs, and a reasonable-care exception. Take advice before answering it., The offering limit aggregates only what was sold in reliance on section 4(a)(6). Sales under other exemptions are not added in. Whether a concurrent offering is integrated with this one is a separate question, which Rule 100(e) refers out to 17 CFR 230.152. and Rules 201(t)(1) and (t)(2) say that if higher-assurance financial statements are already available, the issuer must provide those instead. That trigger turns on what your company happens to hold, and is not modelled here..

<!-- l4: decide:law as in force -->

**31.** Law as in force means 17 CFR Part 227 as in force on 2026-07-23. The dollar figures are adjusted for inflation on roughly a five-yearly cycle; the last adjustment took effect 2022-09-20 and the next is due around 2027..

