<!-- l4: decide:while the duty runs you must -->

**44.** While the duty runs you must means list of concatenate File a Form C-AR annual report within , days to file the annual report after fiscal year end as string and  days of the end of each fiscal year, and post it on your website (17 CFR 227.202(a), 227.203(b)(1)). and concatenate When one of the five conditions occurs, file a Form C-TR within , business days to file Form C-TR as string and  business days. Until you do, the duty stands (17 CFR 227.203(b)(3))..

<!-- l4: decide:reporting caveats -->

**45.** Reporting caveats means list of concatenate The Form C-TR deadline is , business days to file Form C-TR as string,  BUSINESS days, and the annual report deadline is , days to file the annual report after fiscal year end as string and  plain days. The corpus counts both in plain days, because the deadline arithmetic has no business-day calendar. Where a weekend or a holiday falls inside the window, the true business-day deadline is later than the count used here., This check answers whether the duty MAY come to an end. It does not end by itself: filing the Form C-TR is what ends it. and Failing to file does not cost you the exemption for an offering already made (17 CFR 227.100(a)(4)), but it does disqualify you from your next Regulation Crowdfunding offering for two years (17 CFR 227.100(b)(5))..

# The exported entry points

<!-- l4: decide:raise check -->

**46. export default Check whether a company can raise money under SEC Regulation Crowdfunding, how much it may raise now, what financial statements it must provide, and what it will owe afterwards.**

In relation to a RaisePlan “plan”, raise check means RaiseAssessment where you can use Reg CF is issuer is eligible with issuer profile from with plan and offering is within the offering limit with offering from with plan, the most you can raise now is headroom left with plan, blockers is blockers for with plan, financial statements you must provide is financial statements required with offering from with plan, why those financial statements is why those financial statements for with plan, what you must still line up is what you must still line up, after you raise you must is after you raise you must, caveats is raise caveats and law as in force is law as in force.

<!-- l4: decide:investment limit check -->

**47. export Work out the most you may invest across all SEC Regulation Crowdfunding offerings in a 12-month period, and how much of that you have left.**

In relation to an InvestorFacts “facts”, investment limit check means InvestmentLimitAnswer where you have no limit is facts's an accredited investor, your 12 month limit is limit if any for with facts, you have already used is facts's invested under Reg CF in the last 12 months, you can still invest is still investable for with facts, we measured against is greater of annual income or net worth with investor profile from with facts, which limb applies is which limb for with facts, how this is worked out is how the limit is worked out for with facts and caveats is investment caveats.

<!-- l4: decide:investment limit under the rules effective on -->

**48. export Work out what an investor's 12-month Regulation Crowdfunding investment limit was, or will be, under the rules in force on a chosen date — for checking a past investment against the rules that actually applied to it.**

In relation to a DATE “rule date” and an InvestorFacts “facts”, investment limit under the rules effective on means EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT with rule date and investment limit with investor profile from with facts.

<!-- l4: decide:resale check -->

